<h1>Likutay Halachos — Inyan Kedushah d'Sidra<br><span style="font-size:18px; color:#7a622e;">Halacha 1 (§1–5)</span></h1>

<p class="no-indent" style="text-align:center; color:#888; font-size:15px; margin-bottom:30px;">Based on LM II:82 — "Ki Saitzai LaMilchamah"<br/>Kaseder &amp; Shelo Kaseder · Lashon HaKodesh &amp; Targum · Tziyon · Mashi'ach</p>

<h3>§1</h3>

<p>The matter of <span class="key-term">Kedushah d'Sidra</span> — the Kedushah of "<span class="transliteration">Uva l'Tziyon</span>" that is recited in Lashon HaKodesh and in Lashon Targum, through which the shefa is drawn below (as brought in the Kavanos):</p>

<p>Based on what Rabbainu z"l wrote in the ma'amar "<span class="transliteration">Ki saitzai lamilchamah</span>" in Likutay Tinyana Siman 82 — study the entire ma'amar well. There are the aspects of <span class="key-term">kaseder</span> <span class="bracket-def">[in order]</span> and <span class="key-term">shelo kaseder</span> <span class="bracket-def">[not in order]</span> — the Alef-Bais and <span class="transliteration">Tashrak</span> <span class="bracket-def">[reverse order]</span> — the aspects of <span class="transliteration">achor vaKedem</span> <span class="bracket-def">[behind and before]</span>. This is <span class="bold-concept">Adam and Chavah</span>: kaseder and shelo kaseder. The Name Havayah with the filling of Alefin = gematria <span class="transliteration">Mah</span> (45) = Adam. Chavah = Malchus/Peh <span class="bracket-def">[mouth]</span> = Torah sheb'al Peh = speech.</p>

<p>The principle: when things go for a person <span class="bold-concept">shelo kaseder</span> — it is because he divides the aspect of Malchus for himself (= gadlus/arrogance: "<span class="transliteration">Ana emloch</span>" — "I will rule"). Then things go shelo kaseder, for he is within the aspect of shelo kaseder (= Malchus/Chavah/Tashrak). But when this aspect of Chavah/Malchus is <span class="bold-concept">connected to HaKadosh Baruch Hu</span> (= Adam), then things go kaseder — for "<span class="transliteration">b'asar d'is d'char</span>" <span class="bracket-def">[where the male aspect is present...]</span>. The aspect of kaseder is called Yud. When one divides the four aspects of Malchus for himself → shelo kaseder → <span class="transliteration">davai</span> <span class="bracket-def">[sickness]</span>: "<span class="transliteration">V'chol laivav davai</span>" — "And every heart is sick" <span class="source">(Y'shayah 1)</span>, for shelo kaseder = heart-sickness: "<span class="transliteration">Tocheles m'mushachah machalah laiv</span>" — "Hope deferred makes the heart sick."</p>

<p>When a person sees that things are going shelo kaseder — he should know he has gadlus → do t'shuvah → lower himself → become Mah → Chavah returns to Adam → kaseder. The essential chiyus of Malchus = Mah = Chochmah (<span class="transliteration">Ko'ach Mah</span>) = the chiyus of everything: "<span class="transliteration">Mah kochainu mah chayainu</span>" — "What is our strength, what is our life"; "<span class="transliteration">HaChochmah t'chayeh</span>" — "Wisdom gives life" <span class="source">(Koheles 7)</span>. "<span class="transliteration">LaHashem ha'aretz um'lo'ah</span>" — "The earth and its fullness belong to Hashem" <span class="source">(Tehillim 24)</span>: when the earth (= Chavah/Malchus) is connected to Hashem → it is in its fullness and completeness.</p>

<p>The essential t'shuvah is in the month of <span class="transliteration">Elul</span> — for then Moshe opened a well-trodden path. Moshe connected himself even to the lowest of the low and gave his life for them. In every ascent he found HaKadosh Baruch Hu there: "<span class="transliteration">Im esak shamayim sham Atah</span>" — "If I ascend to heaven, You are there" — this is the secret of the Kavanos of Elul.</p>

<h3>§2</h3>

<p>This is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Kedushah d'Sidra recited after tefillah</span>. Tefillah = Malchus/Peh: "<span class="transliteration">Adoshem s'fasai tiftach</span>." The essential completeness of tefillah = connecting and unifying tefillah with Hashem in complete unity. Whoever merits tefillah properly in completeness — the tefillah is simple unity with Hashem: "<span class="transliteration">Hu t'hilasecha v'Hu Elokecha</span>" — "He is your praise and He is your God." Such tefillah is certainly accepted: "<span class="transliteration">V'hayah terem yik'ra'u va'Ani e'eneh</span>" — "Before they call, I will answer" — and his request is fulfilled immediately. When tefillah (= shelo kaseder/Chavah/Malchus) is included in kaseder (= Adam/HKB"H) → everything becomes kaseder → all requests fulfilled: "<span class="transliteration">Y'malai Hashem kol mish'alosecha</span>" — "May Hashem fulfill all your requests" <span class="source">(Tehillim 20)</span>.</p>

<p>But one who does not merit his tefillah being included in Him — due to <span class="transliteration">machshavos zaros</span> <span class="bracket-def">[foreign thoughts]</span> in tefillah (= p'niyos/gadlus = "<span class="transliteration">Ana emloch</span>" — dividing Malchus for himself) → shelo kaseder → tefillah not accepted → request not fulfilled = "<span class="transliteration">tocheles m'mushachah machalah laiv</span>." Therefore he must do t'shuvah, lower himself → return to Mah → shelo kaseder is included in kaseder → request fulfilled → kaseder.</p>

<p>This is <span class="bold-concept">Kedushah d'Sidra after tefillah</span>: to draw the shefa. To draw the shefa that comes through tefillah (= fulfilling one's request) — the aspect of shelo kaseder must be nullified, returned and included in kaseder. Therefore we say Kedushah d'Sidra → shelo kaseder included in kaseder. <span class="key-term">Kadosh</span> = Chochmah: "<span class="transliteration">Kodesh Yisrael laHashem raishis</span>" <span class="source">(Yirmiyah 2)</span>, and "<span class="transliteration">Raishis Chochmah</span>" <span class="source">(Tehillim 111)</span> — Kodesh = Chochmah = Mah/Adam. "<span class="transliteration">Atem k'ruyim Adam</span>" — "You [Yisrael] are called Adam" = Mah = Chochmah = Kadosh. "<span class="transliteration">Yisrael alah bamachshavah t'chilah</span>" — "Yisrael arose in thought first" = Chochmah (thought = Chochmah). Kedushah = Chochmah/Mah/Adam = kaseder. This is the aspect of the <span class="transliteration">yud minay k'dushah</span> <span class="bracket-def">[ten types of holiness]</span>.</p>

<p>"<span class="transliteration">Ain k'dushah b'fachos mai'asarah</span>" — "There is no kedushah with fewer than ten" — kedushah = kaseder = Yud <span class="bracket-def">[= ten]</span>. We recite the Kedushah in <span class="key-term">Lashon HaKodesh and Lashon Targum</span>. Lashon Targum = shelo kaseder = Chavah, whose essential construction was through <span class="transliteration">tardaimah</span> <span class="bracket-def">[deep sleep]</span>: "<span class="transliteration">Vayapail Hashem Elokim tardaimah</span>" <span class="source">(Beraishis 2)</span>. <span class="transliteration">Tardaimah</span> = the numerical value of <span class="transliteration">Targum</span>. Lashon HaKodesh and Lashon Targum (from which the seventy languages draw) = kaseder and shelo kaseder. The essential ordering of language is Lashon HaKodesh — through which the world was created — the true, properly ordered arrangement = kaseder. The arrangements of other languages = shelo kaseder = "<span class="transliteration">lashon ilgim</span>" <span class="bracket-def">[stammering tongues]</span> (incomplete, not ordered according to the six days of Creation).</p>

<p>Therefore we recite Kedushah d'Sidra in Lashon HaKodesh and Lashon Targum — so that Targum (= shelo kaseder) is included within Kodesh/Lashon HaKodesh (= kaseder/Chochmah). This is why it is called "Lashon <span class="bold-concept">HaKodesh</span>" — because this language is included in kaseder = Kadosh. Now we include also Lashon Targum (source of the seventy languages = shelo kaseder = tardaimah) within Kodesh/Lashon HaKodesh → shefa drawn → all heart's requests fulfilled → through shelo kaseder being included in kaseder. Therefore it is called "<span class="key-term">K'dusha d'Sidra</span>" — "<span class="transliteration">d'Sidra</span>" specifically — because the essence of this Kedushah is to make everything <span class="transliteration">kaseder</span> → heart's requests fulfilled = the descent of shefa at Kedushah d'Sidra.</p>

<h3>§3</h3>

<p>This is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">three k'dushos</span> corresponding to the three Alefin in the Name Mah (= Adam). This is: "<span class="transliteration">Kadish bishmay m'roma ila'ah bais sh'chintaih, kadish al ar'ah</span>" — "Holy in the heavens above, the dwelling of His Sh'chinah; holy upon the earth" — the aspect of the t'shuvah above: "<span class="transliteration">Im esak shamayim sham Atah v'atzi'ah sh'ol hineka</span>" — "If I ascend to heaven, You are there; if I make my bed in the grave, behold You." This itself is Kadish in the highest heavens, Kadish upon the earth. "<span class="transliteration">M'lo chol ha'aretz K'vodo</span>" — "The fullness of the whole earth is His Glory" = "<span class="transliteration">LaHashem ha'aretz um'lo'ah</span>" — Kedushah drawn upon Malchus/Eretz → it is in fullness and completeness → Malchus/Eretz included in kaseder/Adam/Kadosh.</p>

<h3>§4</h3>

<p>This is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Ashray</span> recited beforehand — "<span class="transliteration">T'hilah l'Dovid</span>" arranged according to the Alef-Bais, containing all twenty-two letters. <span class="transliteration">T'hilah l'Dovid</span> = Malchus/Peh — so that it will be included in the Alef-Bais kaseder through Kedushah d'Sidra.</p>

<h3>§5</h3>

<p>This is the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Uva l'Tziyon Go'ail ul'shavay fesha</span>" — "A redeemer comes to Tziyon and to those who repent from sin." In <span class="transliteration">Tziyon</span> — where the Bais HaMikdash and Kodesh Kodashim stood — all ten types of kedushah of Eretz Yisrael are included. Therefore Tziyon is the <span class="transliteration">Sha'ar HaShamayim</span> <span class="bracket-def">[Gate of Heaven]</span> through which all tefillos ascend. The world in its totality, vis-à-vis Hashem, is in the aspect of shelo kaseder (= Tashrak: "<span class="transliteration">b'Tishray nivra ha'olam</span>" — "In Tishray the world was created" — Tishray = Tashrak). Kaseder = Mah; the world = <span class="transliteration">yaish</span> <span class="bracket-def">[existence/something]</span> = shelo kaseder (the world is governed through Malchus = shelo kaseder).</p>

<p>The essential chiyus and existence of the world is through the world being included in His Kedushah — through Yisrael K'doshim who sanctify themselves and the world → the world is included in kaseder (= Kodesh) = the essential chiyus. The essential chiyus and existence of the world is through Eretz Yisrael where all ten types of kedushah exist — kedushah above kedushah (the Haichal holier than the rest, until <span class="transliteration">Lifnay v'Lifnim</span> <span class="bracket-def">[the innermost chamber]</span> = Kodesh Kodashim). The <span class="key-term">Even Sh'siyah</span> <span class="bracket-def">[Foundation Stone]</span> — the tenth and highest kedushah, containing all ten types — is the point from which the world was founded. This point has no physical dimension — it is in the aspect of Mah. This point (containing all ten types of kedushah) is included in Mah = Chochmah = Kodesh. Therefore the essential ascent of all tefillos is through the Even Sh'siyah — through there, tefillos (= shelo kaseder) are included in Mah (= kaseder).</p>

<p>Therefore in Kedushah d'Sidra we mention the <span class="bold-concept">kedushah of Tziyon</span>: "<span class="transliteration">Uva l'Tziyon Go'ail</span>" — for the essential inclusion of shelo kaseder in kaseder (= Kedushah d'Sidra) is through Tziyon, where the Even Sh'siyah stands, through whose point tefillos ascend into Mah/Kadosh.</p>

<p>"<span class="transliteration">Uva l'Tziyon <span class="key-term">Go'ail</span></span>" — for the essential aspect of kaseder will be at the coming of the Go'ail Tzedek speedily in our days. Now everything runs shelo kaseder — Yisrael are below in lowliness and the nations are in greatness, contrary to the proper order. But when <span class="bold-concept">Mashi'ach comes → everything will be kaseder</span>: Yisrael above, and among Yisrael itself, whoever is closer to Hashem in truth will be in greatness and goodness (unlike now, when things run shelo kaseder). Therefore we mention "<span class="transliteration">Uva l'Tziyon Go'ail</span>" in Kedushah d'Sidra — to arouse the sparkling of Mashi'ach, to draw even now the aspect of kaseder = shefa, berachah, and goodness.</p>

<p class="no-indent" style="margin-top:30px;text-align:center;color:#888;font-size:14px;font-style:italic;">Note: The remaining halachos discussing Kedushah d'Sidra are included in Hilchos N'filas Apayim.</p>

<div style="margin-top:50px;padding-top:20px;border-top:2px dashed #c8a96e;">
<p class="no-indent" style="text-align:center;font-size:20px;color:#7a622e;font-weight:bold;margin-bottom:5px;">Translator's Overview</p>
<p class="no-indent" style="text-align:center;font-size:13px;color:#999;margin-bottom:20px;">The following summary and diagram are not part of the original text.</p>

<p class="no-indent" style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;">This halacha maps LM II:82 onto the liturgical structure of Kedushah d'Sidra. The core teaching: all of reality divides into kaseder (in proper order) and shelo kaseder (out of order). Kaseder = Adam = Mah = Chochmah = Kodesh = humility; shelo kaseder = Chavah = Malchus = gadlus/arrogance = "I will rule." When Malchus is connected to Hashem → kaseder → everything goes well; when severed by gadlus → shelo kaseder → "tocheles m'mushachah" (hope deferred = heart-sickness). Kedushah d'Sidra (recited in both Lashon HaKodesh and Targum) includes shelo kaseder within kaseder — drawing shefa. The three Kadosh-es correspond to the three Alefin in the Name Mah. Tziyon/Even Sh'siyah = the point where all tefillos ascend from shelo kaseder into Mah. "Uva l'Tziyon Go'ail" = Mashi'ach, when everything will finally be kaseder.</p>

